    {
      "id": "concept-veronica-bloody-mary-mirror-ritual",
      "kind": "concept",
      "promptEs": "Verónica · dos espejos · repetir el nombre",
      "questionEn": "Why does the Spanish comic invoke Verónica and then show many matching figures?",
      "answerEn": "The translation substitutes Verónica, a name used for a Spanish mirror legend, for the official comic's Bloody Mary. The two facing mirrors multiply the reflections, and the joke turns those reflections into many summoned figures.",
      "noteEn": "The ritual normally centers on repeating one frightening name before a mirror. The comic adds a second mirror so the reflected copies appear to repeat the invocation too.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Dos espejos enfrentados producen muchas imágenes repetidas.",
        "en": "Two facing mirrors produce many repeated images."
      },
      "tags": [
        "concept",
